<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Required to send Apple Events, which is how an app is launched in the
	     background and how some controls are driven. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>

	<!-- Deliberately absent, and each absence is a decision:

	     com.apple.security.app-sandbox
	       A sandboxed process cannot hold Accessibility or drive other apps.
	       Sandboxing this helper would make it unable to do the only thing it
	       exists to do.

	     com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory
	     com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
	     com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables
	       Each of these is a way for another process to get its own code
	       running inside a binary that holds Accessibility and Screen
	       Recording. That is precisely the thing worth preventing here, so the
	       hardened runtime keeps its defaults.

	     com.apple.security.network.client
	       The helper never talks to the network. It reads windows, sends
	       events, and answers on stdio. Nothing it holds should be able to
	       leave the machine on its own initiative. -->
</dict>
</plist>
